// **What `src/generators.c` actually hands a generator.** The one test the C-to-Ziman boundary
// has never had, and the reason three bugs shipped through it in a week: every other fixture
// builds its `meta.Decl` with `meta.generic(..)` by hand, so it asserts what a *generator* does
// with a type and cannot see what *reification* produced.
//
// `#[derive(Reflect)]` (lib/core/derive_reflect.zm) prints the declaration and generates
// nothing, so the expected output below is reification's own answer, byte for byte.
//
// **Some of what it records is wrong, deliberately.** `Result`, `Channel` and `fn` arrive with
// `args=0` and the whole type stuffed into `name`; `Option` arrives as `kind=struct` here and
// as `kind=enum` elsewhere. Those are the defects docs/design/meta.md §3 names and §5 fixes --
// pinned now so that the fix shows up as a diff in this file rather than as a claim.
//
// Covers every kind in that §5 table: the nine scalars, array, set, map, the three flat ones, a
// type variable, a generic struct, a qualified name inside an `Option` (the stripped-qualifier
// bug), and an enum with and without payloads.
use time
use uuid.Uuid

#[derive(Reflect)]
struct Scalars {
    a: int
    b: float
    c: bool
    d: string
    e: bigint
    f: decimal
    g: byte
}

#[derive(Reflect)]
struct Collections {
    items: [string]
    names: Set<string>
    scores: Map<string, int>
    nested: Map<string, [Option<int>]>
}

// The three the model still flattens, and a type variable.
#[derive(Reflect)]
struct Flat<T> {
    r: Result<int, string>
    f: fn(int) -> string
    c: Channel<int>
    v: T
}

// A module-qualified name, written both ways: `time.Instant` with `use time`, and `Uuid`
// imported by name. The qualifier each one keeps is the thing the 2026-10-28 bug got wrong, and
// it only reaches generated text through a wrapper like `Option`.
#[derive(Reflect)]
struct Qualified {
    bare: Uuid
    qualified: time.Instant
    wrapped: Option<time.Instant>
    listed: [time.LocalDate]
}

// A **bounded** type parameter too: `type_params` is a list of bare names, so the `: Hash` is
// dropped. docs/design/meta.md §9 says that is deliberate -- this is where it is visible.
#[derive(Reflect)]
struct Generic<T: Hash, U> {
    one: T
    pair: Map<T, U>
}

#[derive(Reflect)]
enum Mixed {
    None
    Int(int)
    Text(string)
    Items([Uuid])
}

#[derive(Reflect)]
enum Wrapper<T> {
    Empty
    Held(T)
    Many([T])
}

fn main() {
    print("ok")
}
